<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>25 years after 9/11: Al-Qaeda weakened but not gone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:681c0fd6a3e5d05b35a2a1058c6dfb000e98bf6864e5f30bdf108f83cff00814</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-weakened-but-not-gone/a-79202457--b51e1f0501b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-weakened-but-not-gone/a-79202457?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">25 years after 9/11, the terrorist group al-Qaeda is no longer the global terrorist organization it once was. Its central leadership has been weakened, but offshoots remain strong across Africa and Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Goethe-Institut is closing in Russia. Russians tell DW how canceled exams are upending their plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beaf92a33b0e4bb231582cab3a4563228b539083d01c835e279e330ac55ef4cd</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-thei/a-79218936--791b0bcb39e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-their-plans/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia affects their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>African Parks: When conservation becomes a question of power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00e5a2d1c24bc59d150512c67bcc6b1902c1ac8c3a270e2aa8f1832daec79f4d</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/african-parks-when-conservation-becomes-a-question-of-power/a-78914372--4689a2636f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/african-parks-when-conservation-becomes-a-question-of-power/a-78914372?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">African Parks is dedicated to protecting wildlife on the continent across some vast areas. But the organization faces allegations of human rights abuses by rangers. Now, Prince Harry is stepping down from its board.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea spends war windfall on arms, infrastructure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d14a037074c84b75fb2413e8f58bb691ad408eadab77bc1dde2dee617c23dc</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-spends-war-windfall-on-arms-infrastructure/a-79218305--540623f7d851.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-spends-war-windfall-on-arms-infrastructure/a-79218305?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ukraine war and Pyongyang's alliance with Moscow have delivered an economic boost to North Korea, allowing the regime to pursue a range of long-desired projects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are electric vehicles really bad for the environment?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31eef617155c534d729513c1622aff56444a1711e5d9209ac67a07cf8103cdd0</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-electric-vehicles-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336--2b5b564fe6cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-electric-vehicles-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some German politicians are calling for a delay to the EU plan to phase out gas-powered vehicles, saying cars must be judged on the entire carbon footprint. But the full picture still says EVs are more climate friendly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar seeks closer foreign ties amid global isolation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c4308156599a4b4ef0d5d5bbd424f43f7b8d6746d5f85c3c90f2d7a40d48707</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T12:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-seeks-closer-foreign-ties-amid-global-isolation/a-79212234--8e8d12e76398.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-seeks-closer-foreign-ties-amid-global-isolation/a-79212234?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Myanmar coup leader Min Aung Hlaing has been on a diplomatic offensive since becoming president in April, but foreign friends may still be few and far between.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China: Cargo ship fire kills at least 25</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a99f20eb89c8a64ad27ede6a5e9aa9834dd6fb1c33fc5172f6e9a0ddfd9fc1e3</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-cargo-ship-fire-kills-at-least-25/a-79212704--ae3b308586a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-cargo-ship-fire-kills-at-least-25/a-79212704?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least five people are missing after a cargo ship caught fire at the port of Qingdao. The cause remains unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc39b2cf321313444f7feb2bd82943d72c9b3e772a731683b7ec3fdf5e0c82fb</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Call in China to end English's core status sparks debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d45551fcea889f351f268db9f370df376b5700779066aa537fcac36597e87435</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629--c3ac5be694ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A call to downgrade English in Chinese schools is fueling discussion over its value for students, careers and China's global competitiveness in the age of AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:359678b7a879278cfecfc96046dcec23543ff3886a63d7ab50c9fd0b79689ae3</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:37Z</updated><